From c9d20fff668f1bc30708369f255a6f2dbbf9dcb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:17:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] USB 2.0 host on one T6050 Type-C port (J716s usbhost DTB)

- patches/linux/0010: phy-apple-usb2, the USB2 half of the Type-C PHY
  (m1n1's bring-up sequence plus the host-mode SIG bits).
- patches/linux/0011: build tipd/ when only SN201202x is enabled.
- patches/linux/0012: sn201202x without SPMI interrupts (gen 4 SPMI).
- dt/t6050-usb-host.dtsi: usb2phy nodes; T6050_USB_HOST_PORT (default 1,
  left-front) becomes dual-role with a role switch starting in host mode;
  the two other ports stay peripheral for the CDC-EEM tether.
- dt/t6050-j716s-usbhost.dts: separate DTB, t6050-j716s.dtb unchanged.
- configs/omarchy-usb-host.config: xHCI, PHY, Ethernet/Wi-Fi dongles,
  UAS, SN201202x, all =y (no modules on the target).
- build-kernel.sh: install the new files, register the DTB (rewriting the
  marker block so existing trees pick it up), merge the fragment, and
  require its key symbols so an old .config is regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>

